WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.392 --> 00:00:02.342
- I don't really think
I've ever really talked

00:00:02.342 --> 00:00:03.770
to my Lyft driver about problems.

00:00:03.770 --> 00:00:05.466
I remember once my Lyft
driver sang with me.

00:00:05.466 --> 00:00:06.844
That was special.

00:00:06.844 --> 00:00:09.902
(upbeat music)

00:00:09.902 --> 00:00:11.641
- Whenever I (speaks off
mic) an Uber a lift for work

00:00:11.641 --> 00:00:12.474
I'd walk in, say, "Hi!",

00:00:12.474 --> 00:00:14.542
and like my phone, right away.

00:00:14.542 --> 00:00:16.716
- I think sometimes I
talk to my Lyft driver

00:00:16.716 --> 00:00:19.158
when I'm drunk, and we
have great conversations.

00:00:19.158 --> 00:00:21.610
- Maintaining a kind of healthy lifestyle

00:00:21.610 --> 00:00:22.711
while really busy at work

00:00:22.711 --> 00:00:24.152
is what I'm goin' through right now.

00:00:24.152 --> 00:00:26.024
- I think I just need like a hobby

00:00:26.024 --> 00:00:28.549
that I'm not trying to
make into like work.

00:00:28.549 --> 00:00:30.254
- I'm really curious and more delve deeper

00:00:30.254 --> 00:00:32.078
into see if maybe there's something

00:00:32.078 --> 00:00:33.497
that I'm not knowing about myself.

00:00:33.497 --> 00:00:34.965
- I think it's just
weird talking to someone

00:00:34.965 --> 00:00:35.798
about my feelings.

00:00:35.798 --> 00:00:37.317
I talk to myself sometimes.

00:00:37.317 --> 00:00:38.568
Let's see how this goes.

00:00:38.568 --> 00:00:41.281
- My name is Cheri Smith,
and I've been driving

00:00:41.281 --> 00:00:43.796
for Lyft, three and a half years.

00:00:43.796 --> 00:00:47.375
I've had people talk
about relationship issues,

00:00:47.375 --> 00:00:49.663
about what he's done, and they just start

00:00:49.663 --> 00:00:51.175
talking about it.

00:00:51.175 --> 00:00:53.845
I'm not gonna like give my opinion.

00:00:53.845 --> 00:00:55.568
I just keep asking questions.

00:00:55.568 --> 00:00:59.094
Once it hits the
airwaves, it becomes real.

00:00:59.094 --> 00:01:01.133
- I'm from New Jersey, originally.

00:01:01.133 --> 00:01:01.966
- Okay.

00:01:01.966 --> 00:01:04.017
- I moved out here for school.

00:01:04.017 --> 00:01:05.234
- So what'd you study?

00:01:05.234 --> 00:01:07.023
- It was business with a marketing focus.

00:01:07.023 --> 00:01:07.856
- Okay.

00:01:07.856 --> 00:01:10.818
- And then I did a job in that for like,

00:01:10.818 --> 00:01:11.686
what like three months,

00:01:11.686 --> 00:01:14.654
and then I realized
quickly that I hated it,

00:01:14.654 --> 00:01:16.754
and I needed to do something creative.

00:01:16.754 --> 00:01:18.319
So it started working, turns out --

00:01:18.319 --> 00:01:22.034
- I try to encourage them
to follow their passion.

00:01:22.034 --> 00:01:24.488
Are you doing this because somebody

00:01:24.488 --> 00:01:26.235
said you had to do this

00:01:26.235 --> 00:01:29.475
or are you doing it because
it's what you really want to do?

00:01:29.475 --> 00:01:32.846
- Right now, it's kind of like
my job is kind of everything,

00:01:32.846 --> 00:01:35.208
just because it's
important to me to do well,

00:01:35.208 --> 00:01:37.672
and like I'm in, like
it's pretty competitive.

00:01:37.672 --> 00:01:40.347
- Take time for a personal life okay.

00:01:40.347 --> 00:01:41.266
- I try to.

00:01:41.266 --> 00:01:42.869
- 'Cause you're young.

00:01:42.869 --> 00:01:44.852
- I feel like the years are
kind of like fleeting away.

00:01:44.852 --> 00:01:45.698
(laughter)

00:01:45.698 --> 00:01:47.781
- No, they're not.
- Yeah.

00:01:50.623 --> 00:01:51.675
- The last few jobs I had,

00:01:51.675 --> 00:01:54.266
I'd approach every single job opportunity,

00:01:54.266 --> 00:01:55.778
afraid that I wasn't good enough

00:01:55.778 --> 00:01:57.559
or I'd like screw up the job,

00:01:57.559 --> 00:02:00.944
and coming here and
being able to do videos

00:02:00.944 --> 00:02:01.967
and make things,
- Right.

00:02:01.967 --> 00:02:03.873
it just felt like, fuck yeah,

00:02:03.873 --> 00:02:05.639
I'm doing something right, you know.

00:02:05.639 --> 00:02:07.129
There's just something
about venting your life

00:02:07.129 --> 00:02:09.404
to a stranger when you know
that there are gonna be

00:02:09.404 --> 00:02:10.670
no repercussions of it.

00:02:10.670 --> 00:02:11.984
It's just nice.

00:02:11.984 --> 00:02:14.030
- So what's your ultimate goal?

00:02:14.030 --> 00:02:14.863
- In life?

00:02:14.863 --> 00:02:16.055
- In life, yes.
- So deep.

00:02:16.055 --> 00:02:18.722
I get in these conversations
with my passengers.

00:02:18.722 --> 00:02:22.047
I like to feel 'em out and
see where they're goin'

00:02:22.047 --> 00:02:23.977
in life, what their goals are.

00:02:23.977 --> 00:02:26.165
- Longtime goal, I really
wanna own restaurants,

00:02:26.165 --> 00:02:29.410
and also, like I'm gay, so
and I really love like film

00:02:29.410 --> 00:02:31.713
and TV shows as well,
so if I could ever like

00:02:31.713 --> 00:02:34.258
produce TV shows and movies
that have like a food

00:02:34.258 --> 00:02:37.074
and queer focus, that'll be like awesome.

00:02:37.074 --> 00:02:38.491
That'd be like the dream life.

00:02:38.491 --> 00:02:40.321
- Sound like you have some good plans.

00:02:40.321 --> 00:02:42.719
- Been told it's like I
have plans A through Z.

00:02:42.719 --> 00:02:43.552
(laughter)

00:02:43.552 --> 00:02:45.616
And hopefully, somewhere
in there they work out.

00:02:45.616 --> 00:02:46.599
(laughter)

00:02:46.599 --> 00:02:48.869
- Well there's this saying,
if you wanna make God laugh,

00:02:48.869 --> 00:02:50.241
tell him your plans.

00:02:50.241 --> 00:02:52.360
(laughter)

00:02:52.360 --> 00:02:56.194
They like the fact that
they can talk to strangers,

00:02:56.194 --> 00:02:59.182
and they can be themselves.

00:02:59.182 --> 00:03:01.045
- Definitely felt a
little bit more relaxed

00:03:01.045 --> 00:03:03.336
after my vent session with Cheri.

00:03:03.336 --> 00:03:04.519
It was like in the middle of the workday,

00:03:04.519 --> 00:03:06.550
so just to be able to take that break

00:03:06.550 --> 00:03:09.119
and then come back to
work was a nice refresher.

00:03:09.119 --> 00:03:10.631
- Throughout the day,
especially when you're working

00:03:10.631 --> 00:03:13.039
so much, you're kind of
like in your own world,

00:03:13.039 --> 00:03:16.180
and she was really open
to talking about anything.

00:03:16.180 --> 00:03:18.279
- And it really depends
on what kind of energy

00:03:18.279 --> 00:03:19.956
you're putting out there.

00:03:19.956 --> 00:03:22.127
If I'm like energetic about it,

00:03:22.127 --> 00:03:24.966
then, yes, they will
open up, and I like that.

00:03:24.966 --> 00:03:27.084
I think they like it too.

00:03:27.084 --> 00:03:31.367
That's why I'm a
five-star driver (laughs)!

00:03:31.367 --> 00:03:33.867
(jazz music)

